<mujoco model="inspire_hand_on_flange_training">
  <!-- ForgeUltra's TRAINING hand geometry as an FR3 end effector, for
       fr3.xml's `end_effector` attachment slot. The sibling of
       inspire_hand_on_flange.xml, which mounts the dex-urdf hand; keep the
       two transforms identical, because the only thing that should differ
       between the two scenes is the hand itself.

       Why a second one exists: the workspace has two independent
       descriptions of the same Inspire RH56, and they disagree about where
       the thumb sits by about 15 degrees of carry. The student policy was
       distilled on this one, and teacher rollouts on the bench say it is also
       the closer match to the physical hand. See
       scripts/make_training_hand_mjcf.py and
       apps/policy_rollout/utils/compare_hand_models.py.

       As in the sibling, this wrapper materialises the fr3_link8 body that
       Menagerie's FR3 lacks, and attaches hand_mount to the flange 10 mm
       along +z with a 180 degree clocking angle. The 10 mm is the thickness
       of the black physical adapter flange. Keep this transform equal to
       hand_flange_xyz/rpy in
       inspire_franka_description/urdf/inspire_franka.urdf.xacro. -->

  <asset>
    <model name="inspire_hand_training" file="inspire_hand_right_training.xml"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="fr3_link8">
      <!-- The point a POLICY ROLLOUT controls: the thumb/index fingertip
           midpoint at the threading grip, in this hand's geometry, which is
           where the number came from in the first place. Keep equal to
           tool_offset_xyz in controllers_policy.yaml and
           controllers_sim_policy.yaml, and to POLICY_TOOL_OFFSET_XYZ in
           apps/policy_rollout/policy_rollout/hardware.py. Group 4 is hidden
           by default: show it with the passive viewer's site_groups:=4.

           The sibling file also carries a `grasp_tcp` site for trajectory
           replay. It is deliberately absent here: that point is the midpoint
           of a closed pinch measured on the dex-urdf hand, and replay does
           not run against this scene. -->
      <site name="policy_grasp_tcp" pos="-0.059067 -0.028773 0.173311"
        size="0.005" group="4" rgba="0.15 0.85 0.35 0.95"/>
      <frame pos="0 0 0.010" quat="0 0 0 1">
        <attach model="inspire_hand_training" prefix=""/>
      </frame>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
